<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lei Áurea</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1888">1888</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Golden Law</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Lei Aurea, or Golden Law, was the law of 1888 that abolished <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slavery">slavery</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brazilian-empire">Brazilian Empire</a>. It was signed by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/isabel-princess-imperial-of-brazil">Princess Isabel</a> while acting as regent for her father <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pedro-ii-of-brazil">Pedro II</a>. Abolition without compensation alienated many slaveholding landowners from the monarchy, contributing to the overthrow of the empire in 1889.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/lei-aurea.jpg" alt="Lei Áurea" width="320" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Senado Imperial · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Lei_%C3%81urea_(Golden_Law).tif" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>The abolition of slavery by the <b>Lei Áurea</b> (Golden Law) of 1888, long overdue on moral grounds, freed the remaining enslaved people without compensation to their owners or any provision for the freedpeople themselves, dealing a severe blow to the slaveholding elite and precipitating the political crisis that…</blockquote><a href="/empire/brazilian-empire">Brazilian Empire · Socioeconomy</a></li><li><blockquote>Brazil’s <b>Golden Law</b> of 13 May 1888, which ended slavery in the last country of the Americas to keep it, has just two articles: the first declares slavery extinct in Brazil, the second revokes all provisions to the contrary.</blockquote><a href="/movement/abolitionism">Abolitionism · At a glance</a></li></ul></section>
